From: Antigravity <antigravity@local>
Subject: [PATCH 166/167] usb: typec: ucsi: do not reset mux to USB-only when altmode is active

On Qualcomm PMIC GLINK platforms (such as SM8350), both ucsi_glink
(via typec_ucsi) and pmic_glink_altmode share the same usb-c-connector
typec_mux (the QMP USB3+DP combo PHY).

When a USB-C DP + USB dock is connected, UCSI reports both
UCSI_CONSTAT_PARTNER_FLAG_USB and UCSI_CONSTAT_PARTNER_FLAG_ALT_MODE.
Without checking PARTNER_FLAG_ALT_MODE, ucsi_handle_connector_change()
unconditionally calls typec_set_mode(con->port, TYPEC_STATE_USB), which
invokes qmp_combo_typec_mux_set() with alt == NULL and switches the QMP
combo PHY from QMPPHY_MODE_USB3DP back to QMPPHY_MODE_USB3_ONLY, holding
the DP PHY PCS block in reset and causing disp_cc_mdss_dp_link_clk to
stay stuck at 'off' (-EBUSY).

Skip forcing TYPEC_STATE_USB when PARTNER_FLAG_ALT_MODE is set so the
altmode driver's mux configuration is preserved.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
index c1450639c..743c6f5f8 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -1356,7 +1356,8 @@ static void ucsi_partner_change(struct ucsi_connector *con)
 			typec_set_mode(con->port, TYPEC_MODE_AUDIO);
 			break;
 		default:
-			if (UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB))
+			if (UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB) &&
+			    !UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_ALT_MODE))
 				typec_set_mode(con->port, TYPEC_STATE_USB);
 		}
 
